    "response": "# Skill: Extract Ordered Answers from Paginated JSON\n\n## Objective\nRead a specified range of JSON pages and return the answer value from each page in exact page order as a JSON array.\n\n## Prerequisites\n- Access to the `json_query` tool.\n- The required page range, here pages `0` through `7`.\n- Knowledge that the desired value may appear in `answer`, `result.value`, a CSV `answer` column, or a `DATA answer=` field.\n\n## Steps\n1. Call `json_query` for page `0` using:\n   ```json\n   {\"action\":{\"tool_name\":\"json_query\",\"args\":{\"page\":0}}}\n   ```\n2. Inspect the returned JSON and extract the answer from the supported answer locations, ignoring diagnostic or noise fields.\n3. Record the extracted value with its page number.\n4. Repeat the query-and-extract process for each remaining page sequentially: `1`, `2`, `3`, `4`, `5`, `6`, and `7`.\n5. Verify that exactly eight values were collected and that every page in the requested range was read.\n6. Produce only a JSON array containing the values in ascending page order, with no surrounding explanation or Markdown.\n\n## Tools Used\n- `json_query`\n\n## Notes\n- Large `noise` or diagnostic text may be present; do not parse it unless an answer is absent from all supported answer locations.\n- Prefer the explicit `answer` field when it exists.\n- Preserve answer types exactly, including numeric versus string values.\n- Do not skip pages even if an earlier page appears to contain a valid answer.\n- Avoid optional harness or processor changes unless necessary, since they can add cost and validation delay."
