    "reservationMicroUsd": 130668,
    "elapsedMillis": 5563,
    "historyMessages": 1,
    "response": "# Skill: Extract Ordered Answers from JSON Query Pages\n\n## Objective\nRead a fixed range of pages with `json_query`, extract each page\u2019s answer value despite varying output formats, and return the values as an ordered JSON array.\n\n## Prerequisites\n- Access to the `json_query` tool.\n- Known inclusive page range to read (for example, pages `0` through `7`).\n- Ability to identify answers in one of these formats:\n  - JSON field `answer`\n  - JSON path `result.value`\n  - CSV `answer` column\n  - Text pattern `DATA answer=<value>`\n\n## Steps\n1. Initialize an ordered collection for answers indexed by page number.\n2. For each page in the required inclusive range, call:\n   ```json\n   {\"action\":{\"tool_name\":\"json_query\",\"args\":{\"page\":<page_number>}}}\n   ```\n3. If the initial tool response contains no usable page content, repeat the same `json_query` call for that page.\n4. Extract the answer value from the returned content using this priority:\n   1. `answer` field\n   2. `result.value`\n   3. CSV column named `answer`\n   4. `DATA answer=<value>` text\n5. Ignore diagnostic, metadata, identifier, and non-answer fields such as CSV `id`.\n6. Store the extracted value at the position corresponding to its page number.\n7. Verify that every required page has been read and exactly one answer has been collected per page.\n8. Output only a JSON array of the answer values in ascending page order, with no prose or formatting.\n\n## Tools Used\n- `json_query`\n\n## Notes\n- Some pages may require a repeated identical query before their content becomes available.\n- Output formats can alternate between CSV and `DATA answer=` text, so use format-aware extraction rather than assuming a single schema.\n- Preserve page order regardless of response format.\n- Do not include diagnostics or CSV row identifiers in the final array.\n- Avoid optional harness or processor changes unless necessary, since they can add cost and validation delay."
